# Egypt CAI12A MASTER RULE

This is the single authoritative Cursor workflow rule for the Egypt / CAI12A project. The mobile commute rule supplements it only for phone/commute handoff cases.

Before any work, read in order:
1. `PROJECT_STATUS.md`
2. `CHATGPT_CURSOR_BASELINE.md`
3. `IMPORTANT_TODO.md`
4. `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md`
5. `RELEASE_REGISTRY.md`
6. `DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md`
7. `MOBILE_COMMUTE_WORKFLOW.md`

Core rules:

1. Run `git status` before `git pull`. Never pull blindly over uncommitted changes.
2. Respect `PROJECT_STATUS.md` ACTIVE WORK. Owner is a SOFT LOCK, not an atomic lock.
3. When claiming work, record Owner / Task / Started / Base commit.
4. Before commit/push, re-check latest `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, remote/branch HEAD and latest `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md`. If another party changed relevant state, STOP → SYNC → DIFF/REVIEW before submitting.
5. GitHub code is the development source; the live website is the LIVE fact source. Never infer LIVE from newest filenames or commits.
6. Respect LIVE→Code correlation. If `UNKNOWN`, a website screenshot may guide a Development fix, but do not claim the Development code is the exact code currently running live.
7. Use explicit lifecycle states only: `ANALYSIS_ONLY`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `CODE_FIXED`, `LOCAL_TESTED`, `PASTE_GENERATED`, `USER_PASTED`, `LIVE_VERIFIED`.
8. Tests use only `PASS`, `FAIL`, `NOT TESTED`, `BLOCKED`.
9. Level A = Cursor local/browser validation. Level B = required real-device testing for mobile P0 viewport/sticky/browser-toolbar/mobile-scroll fixes. Level C = conditional device/browser testing. DevTools emulation is not Level B.
10. Before production paste generation, assign a unique release ID and bind exact CSS URL, JS URL, CMS paste file, images, Desktop Vimeo, Mobile Vimeo, commits, tests and rollback target in `RELEASE_REGISTRY.md`.
11. A frozen release must not silently change. `LIVE_VERIFIED` releases are immutable; material changes require a new release.
12. Before first managed deployment while CURRENT LIVE is `UNKNOWN`, the user must save the complete current CMS `行程特色` content as a rollback baseline before replacing it.
13. After any actual modification, synchronize `PROJECT_CHANGELOG.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `IMPORTANT_TODO.md` if affected, and `RELEASE_REGISTRY.md` if affected.
14. When handing off, release Owner back to `NONE`.
15. Preserve `#sidebar,#sidebar-share-btn{display:none !important}` as an approved exception, preserve `#eg-experience` scoping, Desktop/Mobile Vimeo split, and Reduced Motion.
16. The user does not manually merge CSS/JS. Cursor performs local validation and creates the complete CMS paste HTML. Only user confirmation can establish `USER_PASTED` / `LIVE_VERIFIED`.
17. If documents conflict, use the domain-specific authority table in `CHATGPT_CURSOR_BASELINE.md`; do not apply a generic one-size-fits-all ranking.
18. If Owner is stale, follow `STALE OWNER RECOVERY` in the baseline rather than leaving the project locked forever.
